The diameter of a wire ST varies linearly with distance along the wire as shown in Fig. 6.1.

{{figure:9702_w18_23_q06_figure_6_1}}

There is a current $I$ in the wire. At end S of the wire, the diameter is $d$ and the average drift speed of the free electrons is $v_{s}$. At end T of the wire, the diameter is $2d$.

On Fig. 6.2, sketch a graph to show the variation of the average drift speed with position along the wire between S and T.

{{figure:9702_w18_23_q06_figure_6_2}}
